"# Implementation Plan - Legal Pipeline Correctness & Execution Fixes\n\nThis plan outlines the changes to resolve issues in `test_legal.py` and `synthesizer.py`.\n\n## User Review Required\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> All changes are backward-compatible and improve accuracy/correctness of the pipeline outputs. No breaking API changes are introduced.\n\n## Proposed Changes\n\n### Legal Pipeline\n\n#### [MODIFY] [test_legal.py](file:///E:/GL_AI/test_legal.py)\n- Reconfigure standard streams (`sys.stdout`/`sys.stderr`) to use UTF-8 to prevent `UnicodeEncodeError` when printing Unicode characters (like `≥`) on Windows environments. *(Completed in quick verify phase)*\n\n#### [MODIFY] [synthesizer.py](file:///E:/GL_AI/src/pipeline/legal_synthesizer/synthesizer.py)\n- **Document Source Cleaning**: Update `_clean_src` to handle `Section unknown` and map document IDs (like `Doc_20260214_...`) to `KPK Forest Ordinance 2002`.\n- **Smart Penalty Extraction**: Upgrade regex scanning to search for species-specific penalties matching terms in the query (e.g. distinguishing Chir Pine's Rs. 98,000 from Deodar's Rs. 206,000).\n- **Clean Conclusion Generation**: Replace character-based slicing (`[:120]` and `[:200]`) with sentence/segment-aware logic to avoid truncated sentences in definition, arrest, and general conclusions.\n\n---\n\n## Verification Plan\n\n### Automated Tests\n- Run `python test_legal.py` to verify all queries execute and output properly without Unicode crashes, incorrect penalties, or truncated conclusions.\n"